Fillets: a line walked into a vanishing end and ended there narrower than
5e-4 of the radius is taken for that end at every radius, instead of being
walked once more into a piece of micrometres of its own (mitcad#1374).

ChFi3d_EndBeforeVanishing (patch 0771) ends a line walked into the vertex
where its rounding vanishes at its first section narrower than 5e-4 of
the radius within a hundredth of the radius of the vertex.
PerformSetOfSurfOnElSpine takes such an end for the end of the stripe
(ContactsAtTangentEnd, patches 0400 and 0771) only where its contacts are within 10 tolesp
(1e-3) of each other: above a radius of 2 the line's end may be wider than
that, and the end was walked once more from there, a second piece of a few
micrometres along the guide, its face a sliver. A boss's foot rounded with
3 or 6 on a plate's top whose side's top edge was rounded first: the
foot's chain runs on along the side's blend's cut on the boss's cylinder
to where that blend vanishes, and the line there ended 1.5e-3 wide at
r = 3: the result had a face of 4e-6 mm2 at each end. ContactsAtTangentEnd
now takes a width up to that of ChFi3d_EndBeforeVanishing, a twentieth of
its reach (a hundredth of the radius) where that is more than 10 tolesp.

Test: geometry/tests/test_fillet_boss_tangent.cpp, the plate's top edge
and the boss's foot rounded together with 3 and 6 on the synthetic bodies
and on the case of MITCAD_GEOMETRY_CASES: no face of the result smaller
than 1e-3 mm2; 24 checks fail without the patch.

Upstream: new.

diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
@@ -4899,8 +4899,13 @@ static bool ContactsAtTangentEnd(const occ::handle<ChFiDS_SurfData>& SD,
   }
   // (Or the section has no width any more, its contacts within Tol of each
   // other, within Reach of V: the walk got no nearer before its sections
-  // got singular.)
-  return P1.Distance(P2) <= Tol && P1.Distance(P) <= Reach && P2.Distance(P) <= Reach;
+  // got singular. Or narrower than the width at which a line walked into
+  // the vanishing end is ended, ChFi3d_EndBeforeVanishing's 5e-4 of the
+  // radius, a twentieth of Reach: at radii above 2 that width is more than
+  // Tol, and the end, not taken for the vanishing end, was walked once
+  // more, a piece of micrometres of its own.)
+  const double aWidth = std::max(Tol, 0.05 * Reach);
+  return P1.Distance(P2) <= aWidth && P1.Distance(P) <= Reach && P2.Distance(P) <= Reach;
 }
 
